{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "ef70b759-1b81-86e3-bf07-1fbb6994455e",
  "created_at": "2026-03-05T10:43:02-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Judith Gifford",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:40:37-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:40:41-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi. Judith Gifford. I'm at 350 Chapel Street. Got my water and sewer bill. I don't understand it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:40:48-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I can walk you through it. What part is confusing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:40:52-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The sewer line. It's higher than the water line. Why? I use water. Sewer is what, going down the drain? Shouldn't it be less?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:00-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can see why it looks that way. The sewer charge is usually based on the water you use, but it's billed at its own rate, and that rate can be higher than the water rate. So the two lines don't match."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:14-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So it's not a mistake."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:17-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not from what you're describing, no. Is the total higher than usual for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Higher. Oh, and the toilet was running constantly last month. Day and night. I fixed it. Maybe that's it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:29-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could well be it. A running toilet can use a lot of water, and the sewer charge follows the usage. If the bill covers last month, that would show up on both lines."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:40-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, so sewer goes up because the toilet ran. Even though it's the same water going down. Okay. No. Hang on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:48-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:50-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry. I'm ironing a shirt. The iron just hissed at me. Okay. So the water I wasted, I pay for twice. Once as water, once as sewer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:41:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a fair way to put it. Both charges are tied to the same usage, just at different rates."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:06-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. Okay. I think I follow. Mostly. Can I pay on a Saturday? City Hall's closed, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:12-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The office is closed Saturdays, but you can pay online any time, and there's a drop box outside City Hall for checks. Either one works on a weekend."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:22-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Online. Where? On the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:25-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There should be a payment web address printed on the bill, or you can find it through the city's website under utilities. Your account number is on the bill too, so have it handy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:36-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Account number. Got it. And the drop box, that's the one by the front door?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:42-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, outside the main entrance. Just make sure the check has your account number on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:48-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. I'm still a little fuzzy on the sewer thing, but I'll look at the bill again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:42:54-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If it still doesn't make sense, call back and we can go through it line by line."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T10:43:00-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks. Bye."
    }
  ],
